00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.360
That's the scientific word for an animal

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.000
that once roamed the Earth, but doesn't anymore

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.540
because they all died out.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.150
The animals become extinct for a few different reasons.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:09.010
This giant lemur megalodipus went extinct because when people arrived at Madagascar,

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:12.410
it was hunted and its habitat was destroyed.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:16.990
There are some animals alive today that are in danger of becoming extinct because their

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.670
numbers are falling so low.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:24.890
Like the hugely impressive African black rhino.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:30.000
Or the beautiful and sleek Ethiopian wolf.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:33.470
intelligent great red ape, the orangutan.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.300
They're what are called endangered species.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.390
If their numbers keep falling and eventually hit zero,

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.420
they would become extinct.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:44.880
Gone from the planet, like these animals of the past.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.480
And we would be left to wonder what it would've been like

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.330
to see them in real life.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.230
